+## Aggregated findings (the other plan reports of the run)
+
+When the run has more plan blocks on (P2, P5, P6, P7, P8: `pipeline_status.py --workspace <worktree>`), they run
+before this review, and this review is the one report that P4 answers. Read each of their documents:
+
+| Block | Document |
+|---|---|
+| P2 | `.context/domain-analysis.json` (the domain packs it selected) |
+| P5 | `.context/findings.jsonl`: the rows with a `rule_ref` (architecture review of the plan) |
+| P6 | `.context/adversarial/adversarial_<slug>*.md` (`Mode: plan-gate`): each `B-n` and `C-n`, unless the verdict is `APPROVE` |
+| P7 | `.context/benchmarks/<task>_plan.json`: the `id` of each must-fix finding |
+| P8 | `.context/deferrals/<task>_deferral-register.md`: `D-n` for row `n` of `## Deferrals rejected` |
+
+Reproduce each finding against the plan. Then add one `## Aggregated findings` section to the review, with one row
+for each id of P6, P7 and P8, and one row for each finding of P2 and P5 that the plan must answer:
+
+```markdown
+## Aggregated findings
+
+| Block | Report | Id | Must-fix |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| P6 | .context/adversarial/adversarial_cd-7_scale.md | B-1 | MF-3 |
+| P6 | .context/adversarial/adversarial_cd-7_scale.md | C-1 | MF-3 |
+| P7 | .context/benchmarks/cd-7_plan.json | cd-7-F01 | MF-4 |
+| P8 | .context/deferrals/cd-7_deferral-register.md | D-1 | MF-5 |
+```
+
+Each `Must-fix` cell is an `MF-n` under your `## Must-fix items`. Two ids that name the same defect can share one `MF-n`.
+Write the item so that it names the id it carries (`MF-3 (P6 B-1, C-1): ...`). A finding that you do not reproduce still
+gets its `MF-n`: write in the item that you did not reproduce it and why, and P4 answers it.
+With an id in the table, the verdict is `READY WITH CHANGES` or `NOT READY`.
+The P3 gate fails while an id of a P6, P7 or P8 report has no row, or while its `MF-n` is not under `## Must-fix items`.
+With this table complete, P4 answers your review alone. In the default run there are no other plan reports: write no table.
